@*
    The reasoning effort something ran at, as a chip after the model's name:
    low, medium, high, xhigh or max. .devbook/design/effort-and-mode-chips.md#effort-chips
    is the rule; this is its drawing.

    Effort is a magnitude, not a state, so the chip rises along one ladder of the
    brand gold rather than borrowing the badge tone scale: low and medium share a
    grey outline, high is gold ink in a gold outline, xhigh adds a gold tint, max is
    solid gold. Low and medium look alike on purpose, which is why the word is
    always the chip's text.

    No effort, no chip. A null or blank value renders nothing at all — not an empty
    chip and not "unknown" — because a chip is a claim that the effort was recorded.
    A host that wants to say "not recorded" says it in its own words beside it.

    A value the ladder does not list is drawn verbatim in the low treatment, and its
    title names the values the ladder expects: flagged, not styled.

    Information, not a control: nothing here is focusable, and the title doubles as
    the accessible name ("Effort: high").
*@
@if (Value is { } value)
{
    <span class="@ClassValue(value)"
          title="@Title(value)"
          aria-label="@Title(value)"
          data-testid="@TestId"
          data-effort="@Step(value)">@value</span>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The steps the ladder draws, lowest first.</summary>
    public static readonly IReadOnlyList<string> Ladder = ["low", "medium", "high", "xhigh", "max"];

    /// <summary>The effort word, as recorded. Null or blank draws nothing.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Effort { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; } = "effort-chip";

    private string? Value => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Effort) ? null : Effort.Trim();

    /// <summary>The ladder step a value takes, or "unknown" for one the ladder does
    /// not list — which draws in the low treatment.</summary>
    public static string Step(string effort) =>
        Ladder.FirstOrDefault(step => string.Equals(step, effort.Trim(), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) ?? "unknown";

    private static string Title(string effort) => Step(effort) == "unknown"
        ? $"Effort: {effort} — not a recorded step; expected one of {string.Join(", ", Ladder)}"
        : $"Effort: {Step(effort)}";

    private string ClassValue(string effort)
    {
        var chip = $"effort-chip effort-chip--{Step(effort)}";
        return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? chip : $"{chip} {CssClass}";
    }
}
